  "how": "craft3d-cli of that commit (a debug build, on the developer's laptop): craft3d-cli run --new '{\"units\": \"mm\"}' --script v71.steps.json --out v71.3dcraft, then craft3d-cli run v71.3dcraft --cmd document.inspect for the features and bodies; two live splines with chord spacing, each closed to a profile by two lines and extruded 2 mm: six points of the line y = x / 2, spaced 1.5, 2.5, 12, 3 and 1 mm apart in x, which chord spacing gives as that line (the ramp's volume is 200, its area 260 + 20 sqrt 5, closed forms), and four points near an involute flank: the spacing of a live spline, format 71. Re-recorded on 2026-11-14 when even spacing was taken out before format 71 left its branch",
